.TH FANCTL 1 "2026" "fan-control" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fanctl \- control the Acer Predator PH315-51 fan mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fanctl
[\fIstatus\fR|\fIfull\fR|\fIauto\fR]
.br
.B fanctl
.BR \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fanctl
is an unprivileged client for
.BR fanctld (8),
a root daemon that writes the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded
controller's fan registers directly. It talks to the daemon over the
Unix socket
.IR /run/fanctld.sock ,
which members of the
.B fanctl
group may use. Add a user with
.B usermod \-aG fanctl
.IR user ,
then log in again.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B fanctl
behaves as if
.I status
was given. It always prints exactly one line of JSON to standard output,
also on errors, so it can feed status bars or
.BR jq (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the fan mode read back from the embedded controller:
\fB{"ok": true, "mode": "auto"}\fR. The mode is \fBauto\fR, \fBfull\fR, or
\fBunknown\fR if the registers hold values set by something else.
.TP
.B full
Force both fans to maximum speed.
.TP
.B auto
Return fan control to the vendor's own curve.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The daemon answered with an error, or its reply could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
The daemon could not be reached: it is not running, or the caller is not
in the
.B fanctl
group.
.TP
.B 64
Invalid command line.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FANCTLD_SOCKET
Socket path to connect to instead of
.IR /run/fanctld.sock .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/fanctld.sock
The daemon's Unix socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fanctld (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Yaroslav Yushchenko
